title: '3. A watermark: one commit of the author''s skgrepo.'
pid: 07c94861-8614-4ba0-ab09-226deaadc81d
body: |2-
  New is what Git names as changed between that commit and the
  worktree, within the region. Cheap: one hash per subscription, and a
  changed path names a changed node, one file per node (though a
  relRepo can put a membership in a second file). But it is all or
  nothing (read half, and the mark cannot move), it needs the author's
  skgrepo under Git, rewritten history loses it, and uncommitted work is
  either always new or never: Ed found most of Jeff's week uncommitted,
  and days of it in one commit called "more".
